# Public, build-time setting. Everything prefixed VITE_ is embedded in the JavaScript bundle that visitors
# download, so NEVER put a secret here (the build fails if a variable name or value looks like one).
#
# Local development: leave this unset. The app calls "/api", which the Vite dev server proxies to
# http://localhost:8000 (see vite.config.ts).
#
# Production (Vercel): set it in the Vercel project settings (Environment Variables) to your deployed backend,
# then REDEPLOY, because the value is read when the site is built:
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://YOUR-SERVICE.onrender.com/api
# The trailing "/api" is added for you if you give only the origin; the backend must list your Vercel URL in its
# CORS_ORIGINS.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=
